kind: graph
semantic_diff: >-
  Gate-2 materiality and the design repair loop, plus set-sized scoping in the
  increment loop, in one graph revision. Counts: 32 nodes / 95 edges / 14 checks
  become 32 / 95 / 15; 5 endpoints and 24 evidence definitions unchanged (three
  evidence subjects reworded). (1) review_campaign_design defines material - the
  nodes that consume the design would build the wrong thing from it as written,
  or a frozen or registered value would move (P9); nothing else. Everything else
  is bookkeeping - recorded in the same findings record, never selecting an
  outcome; the lead applies it as direct edits to the plan or record with one
  revision-log line and the edit plus new digest in run state, no seat and no lap
  (pave-spec 9.4 and the 9.8 lead-edit row). No new outcome or edge is needed:
  bookkeeping never routes, so an outcome for it would be an edge nobody
  traverses. The reviewer labels each material finding's class (repair-introduced
  included) and surfaces so both lead-evaluated checks stay mechanical. (2) New
  check design_loop_within_bound (mechanical, lead) on the four repair edges out
  of the gate - design_findings_to_redesign, narrow_registration_repair,
  narrow_record_repair, narrow_plan_repair - bounds the loop at eight rounds
  without design_sound or two consecutive rounds half repair-introduced, counted
  since the last verbatim user decision at the gate or the last entry from outside
  the design boundary. Repair-introduced is decidable from the block diff plus
  the findings record - a finding on a block the previous lap's block diff
  touched that no earlier round named - and is not assigned in the round after a
  whole-plan lap. Its on_failure_route is the gate itself, re-entered for the
  user's disposition - the lead presents the standing findings with a
  close-anyway recommendation and the user's verbatim decision disposes of them
  (design_sound) or grants one more lap under a fresh count; a P9 finding is
  never disposed. Which seat, if any, answers that re-entry is runtime binding
  and is declared in the binding successor.
  (3) design_approved_by_user states the standing approval - a recorded gate-2
  approval holds across re-entries while the registration is byte-unchanged,
  the criteria and the user decisions recorded at this gate intact, and no
  material finding stands - and the gate
  node's purpose says it applies that standing approval on such a re-entry
  instead of re-asking; batch_review_current's wording follows the layout
  reference (one findings record per review node, a dated section per round),
  no change to what it tests. (4) Outcome
  meanings: design_sound absorbs applied bookkeeping and the bound disposition;
  material_findings names when the full lap is required; narrow_findings drops
  the first-run artifact path and provenance stamp and says the repair is
  block-scoped with a block diff handed back; narrow_delta_scoped counts material
  findings only. (5) draft_increment_plan authors against the target artifacts on
  disk and re-enters block-scoped - the brief names blocks, the lap hands back a
  block diff with touched and must-hold digests, an unnamed-block cascade stops
  for a re-brief, a whole-plan lap is its own briefed lap; increment_plan_draft
  and plan_drafted carry the block diff. (6) scope_next_increment may select a
  set of pending items sized by the batch review's complexity call (one when any
  is complex, up to three low-complexity in aggregate), marks a
  pairwise-disjoint-surface set eligible for concurrent realization, and
  collapses a landed item's plan block to its ledger row; increment_lap_record
  (which also lists any join conflict of a concurrent-eligible set as a scheduling
  defect) and increment_selected carry the set. realize_increment realizes the
  item or set with per-item evidence, converges the set at one outcome by the
  existing precedence, admits one checkout per item on the campaign branch for a
  concurrent-eligible set in its purpose and allowed_effects, and leaves
  hands-per-set to runtime binding. (7)
  verify_run_preconditions records the GPU baseline as a declared input;
  reachability is capture_baseline_reference's baseline_unusable door. (8)
  Rationale-only: the three narrow edges and the three re-entry instrument
  paragraphs drop their user-directed-amendment stamps and the approvals/ path
  (revision 1's deferred item). Price per run: nothing new is priced - a drafter
  lap and a reviewer round per bookkeeping finding go to zero, the design loop is
  capped at eight reviewer rounds per user decision, and one scoping lap may
  carry up to three low-complexity items. Envelope (rule 6) -
  changed_with_approval: the lead gains a write path into the increment plan and
  design record (bookkeeping edits, landed-block collapse), a state-authority
  move; the user gate fires less often under the standing approval, a
  user-directed check change; design_sound can be recorded by user disposition
  at the bound; and realize_increment's write set widens to one checkout per
  item for a concurrent-eligible set. Check strength otherwise never weakens - narrow_delta_scoped
  keeps its recurrence clause, P9 stays non-waivable, no check is dropped. Why
  it holds in general: a repair loop with no declared bound stops only when a
  person tires; a finding the consumer re-derives from persisted inputs cannot
  change what gets built, so a seat that repairs it buys nothing; a realization
  lap that holds one item while disjoint low-complexity items wait pays a
  scoping lap per item for no evidence.
envelope_check: changed_with_approval
plan_evidence: verified
usage_evidence: field
changelog_entry: >-
  Revision 3 (graph): gate-2 materiality (wrong build or frozen value moves),
  bookkeeping as lead edits, a declared design-loop bound with the user as the
  stop, standing gate-2 approval, block-scoped drafter re-entry, set-sized
  scoping with concurrent-eligible disjoint sets, the GPU baseline as a declared
  input, and the deferred stamp and path strip. Field evidence from the first
  run: gate 2 ran 18 reviewer rounds before the user closed it by hand; 49
  drafter laps, 12 pure churn and 22 mixed with about 37 percent of findings
  repair-introduced; 35 review rounds ran before the target configuration
  existed on disk; the gate-2 approval was re-asked after narrow repairs; 51
  scoping laps each selected exactly one item. Checks 14 -> 15; nodes and edges
  unchanged.
